      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary angiography has many limitations for the assessment of coronary artery disease. Intracoronary ultrasound imaging may overcome some of these limitations by providing direct visualization of the luminal area. This report describes a case where intracoronary ultrasound imaging was useful for correct assessment of left main coronary artery disease which enabled avoidance of coronary artery bypass grafting in this patient. Intravascular ultrasound may be a good complement to coronary angiography in selected cases of left main coronary artery lesion."},
